  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe site tests ran only in the `site` job of `release.yml`, after the tag. They were red at three cuts in a row. This PR makes the site green again and runs the site tests in the gate, before the tag.\n\n1. Site (commit 1, `fix(site)`): the site tests were red on `origin/main` 39298012.\n   - The ribbon labels moved from `panes.rs` to `panes/cmd.rs` (#4393). `New tool…` moved to `tool_library_dialog/list_header.rs`. The two tutorial tests now read the files that draw the labels. The assertion is the same.\n   - `site/static/icons/op-rotary-contour.png` and `op-rotary-parallel.png` drifted from `assets/ui/`. They are copied from `assets/ui/`.\n   - The post reference had no row for `manualToolChange` (#4085). The row is new, written from our own contract in `assets/posts/AGENTS.md`.\n2. Gate (commit 2, `fix(gate)`): a step kind that does not start cargo, `xtask/src/site_step.rs`.\n   - The step `site tests (python unittest, zola, node)` runs `python3 -m unittest discover -s site/tests` (else `python`) at the root. It sets `ZOLA` (else `zola` on PATH), `PYTHONUTF8=1` and `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1`. `node` must be on PATH. All calls go through `std::process::Command` with clear errors, under the gate watchdog.\n   - batch and release: always. quick: when the diff touches a path of `site_step::INPUTS`. A quick fallback to batch gets it too.\n   - `Step` has a new field `site: Option<Missing>`. `Run::execute` sends such a step to `site_step::execute` (one line). The step shares the lanes, and `gate batch --lane N/M` gives it to one lane.\n   - `site_step::INPUTS` is the one list of inputs: `site/`, `assets/ui/`, `assets/posts/`, `assets/machines/`, `examples/`, `crates/ui/src/egui_app/`, and the exact source files that the site tests open.\n   - Usage text and the `gate` skill name the step in each tier.\n3. Decision: `docs/decisions/4133-site-tests-in-the-gate.md`.\n\n## The site tests on main, before and after\n\n| Tree | Tools | Result |\n|---|---|---|\n| `origin/main` 39298012 | zola 0.23.6, no node | 112 tests, 23 failures, 6 errors (the 6 errors are node missing) |\n| `origin/main` 39298012 | zola 0.23.6, node 22 | 112 tests, 23 failures |\n| this head | zola 0.23.6, node 22 | 112 tests, OK |\n\n## The missing-tool rule\n\n- quick and batch: a missing tool (python 3, zola, node) is a `SKIP` row. The note is `SKIPPED (tool missing: <tool>) - not a pass; install: ...`. The run does not fail for it, but the row is never `ok`.\n- release: a missing tool is a `FAIL` row. The note names the tool and its install step. The cut gate is the last check before the tag.\n- A zola that is not the pinned 0.23.6 adds a note to the row. It does not fail.\n\n## What the runners need (for the maintainer)\n\nThis PR changes no workflow, no trigger and no runner. Each self-hosted runner user needs these tools on its PATH:\n\n- cut runner (`camcraft-cut`): python 3, zola 0.23.6 (or `ZOLA=<path>` in the runner `.env`), node. The zola download and its sha256 are in `release.yml`, step \"Install pinned Zola\". Without these tools, the cut gate is red at the site step. That is the rule of this PR.\n- post-merge runner (`camcraft-post-merge`): the same tools. Without them, the batch summary shows a `SKIP` row for the site step.\n\nFollow-up: #4433. `post-merge-skip.sh` skips a push that changes only `site/static/`, `site/tools/` or `site/templates/`. That is a `.github` change for the maintainer.\n\n## Pins (xtask)\n\n- `site_step_tests::each_path_that_a_site_test_names_is_an_input`: reads each path literal of `site/tests/*.py` (and the `UI + \"...\"` joins) and fails when `INPUTS` does not cover it.\n- `site_step_tests::input_rule_takes_directories_by_prefix_and_files_exactly`\n- `site_step_tests::batch_and_release_run_the_site_step_with_their_missing_tool_rule`\n- `site_step_tests::quick_runs_the_site_step_only_when_an_input_changed`\n- `site_step_tests::a_missing_tool_is_a_skip_row_in_quick_and_batch_and_a_fail_row_in_release`\n- `site_step_tests::dry_run_prints_the_command_and_the_rule_and_runs_nothing`\n- `site_step_tests::the_note_reads_the_unittest_summary`\n- `tests::batch_skips_slow_binaries_and_release_runs_everything` (updated: batch ends with the site step, release has one more step)\n\n## Gate results on this head\n\nHead `9ca89a5ceb7c288b19f552ca44b182bc0ee566b5`, Linux, `-j 6`:\n\n- `cargo test -j 6 -p xtask`: green (381 unit tests and all integration binaries). This is the quick plan step `xtask unit tests`.\n- `cargo clippy -j 6 -p xtask --all-targets -- -D warnings`: green. It was red on Rust 1.100 at `unit_sweep::plain_dir` (`needless_bool`, a false positive of a `#[cfg(windows)]` block); the function is now one expression on each OS, with the same logic.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main --dry-run`: 2 steps, `xtask unit tests` and `site tests (python unittest, zola, node)` (the diff touches `site/`).\n- `cargo xtask gate batch --dry-run` and `gate release --no-snapshots --dry-run`: each prints the site step and its rule.\n- `cargo xtask gate batch --only \"site tests\"` with zola 0.23.6 and node 22: `ok 18s ... Ran 112 tests in 16.631s, OK`.\n- The same without zola and node: `SKIP ... SKIPPED (tool missing: zola, node) - not a pass; install: ...`, exit 0.\n- `cargo xtask gate release --only \"site tests\"` without zola and node: `FAIL ... tool missing: zola, node - the release tier needs it; install: ...`, exit 1.\n- No light lane and no example catalog suites: no post, toolpath or crate code changed.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- Windows and macOS: the code uses only `std::process::Command` and `/`-free arguments, but it was not built or run there.\n- The cut runner and the post-merge runner: not run. Their tools are not verified.\n- The `--lane N/M` form was not run for real (pinned by `lane_split::assign` in a test).\n\nProcess change: yes\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nChangelog: none\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nFixes #4133\n",
